---
/*
  A component render, shipped in both schemes.

  Both PNGs are in the markup and CSS shows one of them, so changing scheme is
  a repaint rather than a network fetch.

  It replaced a JS `src` swap that, for every specimen on the page, built a new
  Image(), waited for its `onload`, and then waited a further 120ms before
  assigning `src`. The home page carries nine of them, so a single toggle fired
  nine independent round trips that each landed at their own moment and flipped
  one image at a time. The 120ms was reserving room for a crossfade that was
  never written: nothing in any stylesheet read the `data-swapping` attribute
  it set, which is the same dead-hook mistake CHECKLIST.md section 7 already
  records for `data-optional-narrow`.

  The toggle was the visible half. The worse half was first paint: the inline
  script in Base.astro resolves `prefers-color-scheme` BEFORE paint, so a
  visitor whose OS is set to light got a light page immediately - while the
  renders were still the `-dark.png` the server had written, and stayed dark
  until the bottom script ran, preloaded each replacement and waited its 120ms.
  Every light-OS visitor saw that on every page load, not only on a toggle.

  Verified 2026-08-16 with the stored choice cleared and the OS set to light:
  page and renders now both come up light, all images already loaded.

  Both schemes load eagerly, which is about 128KB more than shipping one. That
  is the cost of the toggle being instant, it is measured against a page that
  already streams a 3.8MB wasm bundle in the background, and these are the
  proof assets rather than decoration.
*/
interface Props {
  slug: string;
  width: number;
  height: number;
  alt: string;
  style?: string;
  /* Dark is the default scheme, so only the dark render is worth prioritising
     for the first paint. */
  priority?: boolean;
}

const { slug, width, height, alt, style, priority = false } = Astro.props;
---
<img
  data-specimen-scheme="dark"
  src={`/img/${slug}-dark.png`}
  width={width}
  height={height}
  style={style}
  alt={alt}
  fetchpriority={priority ? 'high' : undefined}
/>
<img
  data-specimen-scheme="light"
  src={`/img/${slug}-light.png`}
  width={width}
  height={height}
  style={style}
  alt={alt}
/>
